\strong{Two-step estimation} (\code{method = "two_step"}) fits the multinomial logit
and then one regression per regime with selection-correction terms:\tabular{lll}{
   \code{correction} \tab Terms per regime \tab Reference \cr
   \code{"lee"} \tab 1 \tab Lee (1983) \cr
   \code{"dmf"} \tab \eqn{J - 1} \tab Dubin and McFadden (1984), with their restriction that the correlations sum to zero \cr
   \code{"bfg1"} \tab \eqn{J} \tab Bourguignon, Fournier and Gurgand (2007), variant without that restriction \cr
   \code{"bfg2"} \tab \eqn{J} \tab the same with normalised disturbances \cr
}


